course: dictionary
lesson: 6119
title: Context and a word with two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A microwave is a kitchen machine that heats or cooks food very quickly. It works with invisible waves, called microwaves, which are a kind of wave like light and radio waves. When you read «Ollie sees a TikTok saying a phone charges if you put it in the microwave for ten seconds», the words the microwave tell you it is the machine, a noun.
explain: Microwave can also be a verb, a doing word. To microwave food means to heat it in a microwave. If someone says «Can you microwave my soup?», they want you to heat it, not to cook it on a stove. Always check: what job is the word doing in this sentence? A machine, or an action?
explain: Context clues also warn you about danger. «Never run a microwave empty, because nothing absorbs the energy and it can be damaged.» The word never tells you this is a rule. Read the clue words, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A microwave is a kitchen machine that heats food very quickly using invisible waves.
fact: Never put metal, foil or some plastic in a microwave, because it can spark.
fact: Food can be very hot inside even when the outside feels cool, so stir it and wait before eating.
fact: Ask an adult before you use a microwave.
exercise: «Ollie sees a TikTok saying a phone charges if you put it in the microwave for ten seconds.» Is this a safe idea? | Yes, if the phone is switched off | Yes, but only for old phones | *No, it is a dangerous idea, so do not try it | Yes, it is a fast way to charge a phone
exercise: On a microwave timer, 1:30 means how long? | One minute and thirty hours | One hour and thirty minutes | Thirty seconds | *One and a half minutes, or 90 seconds
exercise: Mum says, «Can you microwave the soup for two minutes?» What does microwave mean here? | To put the soup in the fridge | To throw the soup away | To eat the soup cold | *To heat the soup in a microwave
test: Which should never go in a microwave because it can spark? | *A metal spoon | Bread | Water in a cup | A plain paper towel
test: Why should you stir the food and wait after heating it? | To make the microwave go faster | *Food can be very hot inside even when the outside feels cool | Because microwaves are slow | To keep the steam in
exam: Why should you never run a microwave empty? | Because the door will not close | Because it uses too little electricity | *Nothing absorbs the energy, so it can be damaged | Because it makes the food taste bad
